{"name":"Light Salome","hex":"#ccf1e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salome","blocks":[{"text":"Salome, also known as Salome III, was a Jewish princess, the daughter of Herod II and princess Herodias. She was a granddaughter of Herod the Great and the stepdaughter of Herod Antipas. She is known from the New Testament, where she is not named, and from an account by the Roman Jewish historian Josephus. In the New Testament, she is known as the stepdaughter of Herod Antipas who demands and receives the head of John the Baptist. According to Josephus, she was first married to her uncle Philip the Tetrarch, after whose death in AD 34, she married her cousin Aristobulus of Chalcis, thus becoming queen of Armenia Minor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Salome_with_the_Baptist%27s_head_-_Charles_Mellin.jpg/330px-Salome_with_the_Baptist%27s_head_-_Charles_Mellin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salome","wikidata":"Q228896"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wilhelm_von_Schadow_-_Salome_z_g%C5%82ow%C4%85_%C5%9Bw._Jana_Chrzciciela_1838.jpg/500px-Wilhelm_von_Schadow_-_Salome_z_g%C5%82ow%C4%85_%C5%9Bw._Jana_Chrzciciela_1838.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wilhelm_von_Schadow_-_Salome_z_g%C5%82ow%C4%85_%C5%9Bw._Jana_Chrzciciela_1838.jpg/1280px-Wilhelm_von_Schadow_-_Salome_z_g%C5%82ow%C4%85_%C5%9Bw._Jana_Chrzciciela_1838.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wilhelm_von_Schadow_-_Salome_z_g%C5%82ow%C4%85_%C5%9Bw._Jana_Chrzciciela_1838.jpg/500px-Wilhelm_von_Schadow_-_Salome_z_g%C5%82ow%C4%85_%C5%9Bw._Jana_Chrzciciela_1838.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Salomé with the head of John the Baptist,Wilhelm von Schadow (1838)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilhelm_von_Schadow_-_Salome_z_g%C5%82ow%C4%85_%C5%9Bw._Jana_Chrzciciela_1838.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Massimo_Stanzione_%281585-1656%29_-_Salome_with_the_Head_of_John_the_Baptist_-_1958.1007_-_Manchester_Art_Gallery.jpg/500px-Massimo_Stanzione_%281585-1656%29_-_Salome_with_the_Head_of_John_the_Baptist_-_1958.1007_-_Manchester_Art_Gallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Massimo_Stanzione_%281585-1656%29_-_Salome_with_the_Head_of_John_the_Baptist_-_1958.1007_-_Manchester_Art_Gallery.jpg/500px-Massimo_Stanzione_%281585-1656%29_-_